Z||000001||Shiner||08-30-2000||11:05 PM||||Putting a later 60* 2.8V6 in your '84 will be almost as much work as putting in a SB Chevy engine.  I don't mean to discourage you, but it's true.<P>------------------<BR>Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-31-2000||12:11 AM||||Anything is possible and I know of a few people who have done this to an '84.  The problem is in '84 the V-6 wasn't even an option.  As such, the wiring wasn't set up for a V-6 either.  You will essentially have to rewire the entire car....not too difficult, but very time consuming.  You'd be better off buying an '85 or newer Fiero or one with a V-6 in it already.  All '85-'88 coupes have the proper wiring for a V-6 install.....it's still not an easy job, but no wiring hassles.||||reg||6
